      "image": null,
      "content": "Prompt injection defenses that rely on another LLM to police the main model often fail under pressure. When an agent processes untrusted inputs like poisoned emails, tickets, or web pages, it can easily be tricked into exfiltrating sensitive data to attacker-controlled destinations.\n\nBouncer takes a refreshingly deterministic approach to this problem. Rather than asking an LLM to judge intent, this Model Context Protocol proxy tracks the source of addresses. If an agent attempts to send an email, share a file, or post data to a destination string that first appeared inside untrusted tool output, the proxy denies the call outright.\n\nIn standard benchmark runs on suites like AgentDojo, this simple invariant cuts off data exfiltration paths cleanly. The trade-off is strictness: completely blocking unknown outbound destinations means legitimate exploratory workflows may require human approval.\n\nDeterministic sandboxing at the protocol layer provides far more reliability than fuzzy semantic guardrails when securing autonomous tools."
