      "content": "Polars 2.1 introduces a major breakthrough for memory-constrained data pipelines: true out-of-core streaming group-by operations with disk shuffling.\n\nWhile Polars previously supported spilling simple operations to disk, high-cardinality group-by aggregations remained a frequent trigger for out-of-memory errors. The engine can now partition intermediate aggregation states, shuffle keys, write spill files to disk when hitting configured memory ceilings, and stream them back to complete processing.\n\nThe release also brings streaming window functions out of core, adds proactive out-of-memory kill threshold controls, and extends SQL execution with recursive CTEs. These additions turn Polars into an increasingly viable, low-footprint replacement for distributed cluster processing on single-node instances handling tens of millions of records.\n\nControlling query-level input/output metrics alongside hard memory budgets provides predictable execution bounds when processing datasets far larger than physical RAM."
