      "image": null,
      "content": "Most multi-agent frameworks treat workflow orchestration like loose scripts, leaving runtime failures to emerge deep inside production runs. Bringing Spring-style dependency injection and compile-time verification to LangGraph agents changes how we structure reliable agentic systems.\n\nAGBoss introduces static verification through Path Scope analysis and decorator-based component wiring. Instead of hoping that downstream actions receive valid tool outputs, the compiler verifies state structural paths ahead of execution. It also introduces transactional LIFO sagas with explicit compensation steps, so when an agent failure occurs midway through an external workflow, previous operations can actually be rolled back safely.\n\nTreating agent architectures with the same architectural rigor as distributed microservices is a huge step forward for production reliability.\n\nType safety and declarative rollback semantics should be baseline requirements for mission-critical agent workflows."
